WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
AI workloads rarely live in one neat place.

2
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:19.590
A team may prototype on developer machines, test on lab hardware, run batch jobs in a private cluster, serve inference from Kubernetes, use managed cloud services for storage or model endpoints, and deploy selected workloads at the edge.

3
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.220
A hybrid AI environment combines these locations, ownership models, and operational assumptions.

4
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:36.310
A single user request may touch an API gateway, authentication service, model-serving route, retrieval service, vector store, cache, database, queue, GPU node, and external service.

5
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:43.110
A failure in any one layer can look like a model problem from the outside.

6
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:53.810
Without enough context, teams may spend valuable time debating whether the issue belongs to the application, infrastructure, data platform, security controls, or a provider dependency.

7
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.860
Clusters add another dimension.

8
00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:05.220
Scheduling, resource allocation, workload placement, node health, accelerator availability, queue depth, and noisy-neighbor effects all influence AI behavior.

9
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:19.820
A model may be correct, but it can still miss latency expectations if it waits too long for a GPU, loads from slow storage, or shares a node with a workload that consumes memory bandwidth.

10
00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:26.230
Hybrid systems also introduce network boundaries, identity boundaries, data movement, and operational ownership questions.

11
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.860
Telemetry should make these layers visible enough for teams to act together.

12
00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.540
The goal is not to collect everything.

13
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:47.020
The goal is to collect the signals that reveal where work traveled, what resources it used, which boundary it crossed, and what changed when behavior became unhealthy.

